From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 16:45:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media (ohos): Report a failure of AVPlayer to the media
 element once

AVPlayer reports a failure through its error callback and by entering
its error state, and the backend sent a player error to the media
element for each. Before the element has metadata, each player error
runs the media data processing failure steps, which queue the error
event, so an element whose resource AVPlayer cannot play could fire
`error` twice. Reading from the media cache made this likely: the end
of the resource now reaches AVPlayer at once, so an empty or
unsupported resource fails within the test of
resource-selection-invoke-pause-networkState.html, which then saw a
second error event. Send only the first of the two.

Fork note: meant for upstream. Drop once upstream has it.

Testing: resource-selection-invoke-pause-networkState.html on OpenHarmony; see Validation.

Validation: a HiHope DAYU200 (OpenHarmony 7.0, API 26), headless release builds of the series. Without this patch, one run of the series' 63 media tests failed resource-selection-invoke-pause-networkState.html with a second error event, and its log shows both player errors; the test passed three times alone with and without the series. With it, two runs of the 63 tests: only the known unexpected OK of autoplay-default-permissions-policy, and one player error in the log of that test.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; written and tested on a device by the agent)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
---
 components/media/backends/ohos/player.rs | 16 ++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/components/media/backends/ohos/player.rs b/components/media/backends/ohos/player.rs
index cdf1464cd72..e6c0282db9a 100644
--- a/components/media/backends/ohos/player.rs
+++ b/components/media/backends/ohos/player.rs
@@ -198,10 +198,11 @@ impl OhosAvPlayer {
                                 let _ = sender_clone.lock().unwrap().send(PlayerEvent::EndOfStream);
                             },
                             AVPlayerState::AV_ERROR => {
-                                errored_clone.store(true, Ordering::SeqCst);
-                                let _ = sender_clone.lock().unwrap().send(PlayerEvent::Error(
-                                    "AVPlayer entered its error state".to_owned(),
-                                ));
+                                if !errored_clone.swap(true, Ordering::SeqCst) {
+                                    let _ = sender_clone.lock().unwrap().send(PlayerEvent::Error(
+                                        "AVPlayer entered its error state".to_owned(),
+                                    ));
+                                }
                             },
                             AVPlayerState::AV_RELEASED => {},
                             _ => {
@@ -336,12 +337,15 @@ impl OhosAvPlayer {
             .connect_error_callback(move |error_code, message| {
                 // AVPlayer also reports operations it does not permit, such as a playback speed for
                 // media it treats as a live stream, or an audio interruption, which don't end
-                // playback. A failure that does also moves AVPlayer to its error state.
+                // playback. A failure that does also moves AVPlayer to its error state, and only
+                // the first of the two reaches the media element.
                 if error_code == OH_AVErrCode::AV_ERR_OPERATE_NOT_PERMIT.0 as i32 {
                     warn!("AVPlayer did not permit an operation: {}", message);
                     return;
                 }
-                errored_clone.store(true, Ordering::SeqCst);
+                if errored_clone.swap(true, Ordering::SeqCst) {
+                    return;
+                }
                 let _ = sender_clone
                     .lock()
                     .unwrap()
